  "hwy.businessRules.section.targhin.intro": "Withdrawal requests, decisions, and negotiation notes.",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.org-membership-transfer.title": "Org membership transfer",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.org-membership-transfer.intro": "Institute-initiated transfer list (legacy OrgMembership).",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.member-list-definitions.title": "Member list definitions",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.member-list-definitions.intro": "hwy_member_list_defs institute vs predicate lists.",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.member-list-legacy-filters.title": "Member list field-by-field filters",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.member-list-legacy-filters.intro": "Toolbar mode 2 (legacy field panel) on Hawiety people lists: row order, membership-id search modes, join-tasjil filter, and server WHERE parity.",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.employees-list.title": "Employees list",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.employees-list.intro": "Studio HWY_Employees_List parity: legacy Read_Employees access, dbo.hwy_employees_list_* reads, and directory identity masks on rows.",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.membership-approval-pipeline.title": "Membership approval (call center & local)",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.membership-approval-pipeline.intro": "Call-center and local verification (Waited_1 / Waited_2): status transitions, activation side effects, and dbo.hwy_membership_apply_* only.",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.nakhebin-linking.title": "Nakhebin linking",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.nakhebin-linking.intro": "Voter link wizard parity through hwy_member_nakhebin_* procedures and Geographic Divisions ids.",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.geo-responsibility-legacy.title": "Geo officials (legacy SP retirement)",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.geo-responsibility-legacy.intro": "Studio geo responsibility replaces H_Circle_* / H_Eghtera_* legacy suggest-approve SPs — single path at cutover.",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.electoral-tree-role-anchor.title": "Electoral tree — one anchor per role",
  "hwy.businessRules.section.electoral-tree-role-anchor.intro": "One person may hold several roles; every electoral-tree role still shares exactly one level and one node — never two places on the tree at once.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-tracking-vs-display.title": "Tracking id vs التياري number",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-tracking-vs-display.body": "Public self-registration tracking is always hwy_members.id (no hwy_tracking_codes table). Staff «membership number» / login UserName is hwy_members.username (COALESCE with base_users.username in vw_hwy_members) and stays empty until local verification approves to active — the tracking id is not substituted into that column.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-display-priority.title": "List column priority (legacy import)",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-display-priority.body": "Legacy ETL and resolveLegacyMemberUsername prefer imported UserName, else legacy TrackingCode on the row. Greenfield pending rows have no التياري until activation; vw_hwy_members.tracking_code exposes member id for search/filters only. Never synthesize m{memberId} or other fake serials for the membership-number column.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-no-synthetic-id.title": "No fake membership numbers",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-no-synthetic-id.body": "Import and repair scripts must not invent a التياري from member id when both legacy UserName and TrackingCode are empty. Runtime lists read username from the member/user join — not auto-generated from id.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-view-coalesce.title": "vw_hwy_members username",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-view-coalesce.body": "Directory username is COALESCE(trim(hwy_members.username), base_users.username) so linked login accounts show the platform username when the member row is blank.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-legacy-editor-semantics.title": "Legacy 2_Approve parity",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-legacy-editor-semantics.body": "Legacy assigned UserName only on approval (HWY_SP_Members_2_Approve), not on first save. AppEndO mirrors that: hwy_self_registration_create_member does not touch hwy_username_repo; dbo.hwy_membership_apply_local_decision (approve → active) allocates from the repo and links base_users when user_id was null.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-unique.title": "Unique pool values",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-unique.body": "hwy_username_repo.username is UNIQUE system-wide. reserved_at is set when a row is tied to a member at activation; released_at optional when a number is returned to the pool.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-allocation-moment.title": "When a number is taken",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-allocation-moment.body": "Only local approve (pending_local → active) selects TOP 1 from hwy_username_repo WHERE member_id IS NULL AND released_at IS NULL ORDER BY NEWID() with UPDLOCK, READPAST — same random-pick intent as legacy repo flags. Operators must seed free rows for new activations; ETL often pre-links member_id for migrated members.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-member-link.title": "Member link at activation",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-member-link.body": "On successful allocation, repo.member_id is set to the activated member and hwy_members.username matches repo.username. ON DELETE SET NULL on member_id keeps historical rows.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-activation-failures.title": "Activation pool errors",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-activation-failures.body": "Local approve with no existing user_id requires a bcrypt password_hash from the app (57106 if missing). Empty pool → 57107. Concurrent claim on the same repo row → 57108. API maps these to operator-facing errors; no silent fallback number.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-skip-when-linked.title": "Skip allocation when already linked",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-skip-when-linked.body": "If hwy_members.user_id is already set (typical after ETL), local approve only updates membership status and membership_on — no second repo pick and no duplicate base_users insert.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-change-log.title": "Dossier timeline",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.username-repo-change-log.body": "After activation, dossier change log reads hwy_member_dossier_change_log_username_repo and emits registration.usernameReserved at reserved_at — not at self-reg submit.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-tracking-code.title": "Applicant tracking code",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-tracking-code.body": "Successful self-reg returns trackingCode = CAST(member_id AS NVARCHAR(32)). dbo.hwy_member_after_create / resend SMS use the same value in template tokens. POST track-by-code resolves status via hwy_members.id (numeric or string), not a separate tracking table.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-identity-required.title": "Four-part name",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-identity-required.body": "first name, father, grandfather, and family name are required on submit (same keys as dossier edit validation).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-national-id.title": "National ID",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-national-id.body": "When filled, national ID must be exactly 12 digits (Iraqi unified number).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-birth-year.title": "Birth year",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-birth-year.body": "Four-digit birth year between 1919 and the current calendar year.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-phone.title": "Mobile phone",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-phone.body": "Phone1 is required; digits only, 11 characters, must start with 07. Phone2 optional with same format.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-referrer.title": "Referrer membership number",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-referrer.body": "Optional referrer username: exactly 6 digits when complete; partial input invalid once typing starts.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-institute-code.title": "Institute code",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.selfreg-institute-code.body": "Optional institute invitation code: 3 digits when provided.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.dossier-note-readonly.title": "Public note field",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.dossier-note-readonly.body": "hwy_members.note is never editable in dossier edit mode (HWY_MEMBER_DOSSIER_NEVER_EDITABLE_MEMBER_FIELDS).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.dossier-staff-notes.title": "Staff notes",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.dossier-staff-notes.body": "Internal commentary uses hwy_member_notes with subject codes — not the public note column.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.dossier-edit-sections.title": "Edit sections",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.dossier-edit-sections.body": "Nested edit URLs allow only basic data (default) and files satellite; institute membership is workflow-managed elsewhere.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.dossier-validation-parity.title": "Validation parity",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.dossier-validation-parity.body": "Studio dossier edit reuses self-registration rules for gender, birth year, province/district, phones, email, and education years.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-gender-limit-source.title": "Gender limit source",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-gender-limit-source.body": "Viewer limits come from session serverContext keys: user.gender_limits, user.hwy_gender_limits, user.GenderLimits, user.gender_view, user.hwy.gender_view, role.gender_limits, role.hwy_gender_limits, role.hwy.gender_view (JSON array or legacy Id objects). When still empty, SQL loads dbo.HWY_Members_GenderLimits for the staff row linked via hwy_members.user_id. isAdmin or genderLimitLegacyIds.length ≥ 2 → no gender mask (legacy JWT GenderLimits count ≥ 2).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-gender-id-mapping.title": "Gender code mapping",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-gender-id-mapping.body": "Member and viewer genders normalize to legacy ids 10011 (male) and 10012 (female) from genderCode values such as 100.1.1 / 100.1.2 or Base Info titles. Comparison uses the first allowed id when only one limit applies.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-gender-phone.title": "Gender-based mask (HashPhones)",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-gender-phone.body": "When a single gender limit applies and member gender differs: firstname → ***** (HWY_MEMBER_IDENTITY_MASK_SENTINEL), non-empty phone1/phone2 → *****, avatarUrl/profile image fields cleared and hasProfileImage false (legacy client picture hide). Runs in applyHwyMemberIdentityFieldMasksToRows after directory enrichment.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-unknown-gender.title": "Missing member gender",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-unknown-gender.body": "Legacy treats empty GenderId as not matching the allowed gender. AppEndO masks phones and first name when genderCode is missing or unmappable under a single-gender viewer limit.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-visible-lineage-fields.title": "Fields left visible",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-visible-lineage-fields.body": "Legacy HashPhones masks FirstName and phones only — not family name, father name, username, or tracking code. AppEndO dossier and lists keep the same lineage/username fields readable unless another rule applies.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-display-full-name.title": "List display name",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-display-full-name.body": "Directory list rows also set displayFullName to ***** when the gender mask applies (stricter than legacy FirstName-only, same privacy intent for grid title column).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-execution-order.title": "Mask order",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-execution-order.body": "Same as legacy: HashPhones first, then HashPhonesForOthers. Institute phone substitution can replace phone1/phone2 even after gender stars.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-institute-membership-eligibility.title": "Institute link eligibility",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-institute-membership-eligibility.body": "approvedRestrictedOrgsCount counts hwy_member_institutes rows with member_accepted = 1, active membership status_code from list scope, and institute_id in {4, 214917, 215103}. orgsMembership STRING_AGG uses titles of all approved institute links on the member (legacy OrgsMembership aggregate).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-institute-phone.title": "Institute ownership mask (HashPhonesForOthers)",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-institute-phone.body": "When approvedRestrictedOrgsCount > 0, phone1 = orgsMembership summary, phone2 empty. Skipped for ADMIN or legacy role ids 1000006 / 1000040 (also platform role name mapping). Bypass roles use substring parity with legacy rls.Contains in JWT roles JSON.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-orgs-notice.title": "Institute membership notice",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-orgs-notice.body": "Dossier view/edit shows an institute membership banner when identityFieldPolicy.institutePhoneMasked is true and orgsMembershipSummary is present on the loaded member row.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-patch-lock.title": "Patch and edit locks",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-patch-lock.body": "getOne attaches identityFieldPolicy. Gender mask locks firstname, phone1, phone2, genderCode; institute mask locks phone1/phone2. Server strips locked fields on PATCH; dossier edit form shows read-only fields and omits locked keys on submit.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-photo-readonly.title": "Photo read-only",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-photo-readonly.body": "personalPhotoReadOnly when gender-masked. UI disables personal_photo edit; POST /api/hwy/member-directory/:id/files rejects personal_photo with 403 when policy forbids upload.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-apply-surfaces.title": "Where masks run",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-apply-surfaces.body": "applyHwyMemberIdentityFieldMasksToRows with viewer session: vw-hwy-members member-directory list/getOne (getOne also attaches identityFieldPolicy), PATCH /api/hwy/member-directory/:id policy strip, org-membership-transfer search, similar-members SP results (genderCode column), member-picker search, profile-nav similar count. List rows are masked but do not ship identityFieldPolicy to the grid client.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-list-cache-viewer.title": "List cache per viewer",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-list-cache-viewer.body": "Directory list GET cache uses cacheByUser (metadata + ensureHwyMemberDirectoryListRuntime pin; dataApiRuntimePolicy forces byUser for vw-hwy-members.hwy-member-directory-list) because masked phones and names depend on the viewer, not only query params.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-deferred-show-phones.title": "Deferred: click-to-reveal phones",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.mask-deferred-show-phones.body": "Legacy list HTML used shared.showPhones to reveal starred phones after click. AppEndO V2 does not implement that UX yet; masked values stay ***** / org text until a future list interaction rule is added.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.files-registration-vs-other.title": "Registration vs other",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.files-registration-vs-other.body": "File kinds split into registration documents (personal photo, ID cards, oath, etc.) and other attachments with separate edit/delete capabilities.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.files-kind-approval.title": "Approval flags",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.files-kind-approval.body": "Core registration kinds use hwy_member_files.is_approved; other_attachment is not approval-gated in the catalog.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.files-registration-approve-sync.title": "Batch approve flags (registration)",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.files-registration-approve-sync.body": "Legacy UpdatePicturesApproveFlags maps to dbo.hwy_member_registration_files_sync_approve_flags (personal photo, national card front/back, voter card front, residence card front) — mutation in SQL, not inline app updates. POST /api/hwy/members/:id/registration-files/sync-approve-flags and dossier files edit approval panel.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.course-status-draft.title": "Draft status",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.course-status-draft.body": "New courses start in draft status code 215114 (HWY_COURSE_STATUS_DRAFT).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.course-send-review.title": "Send to documentation",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.course-send-review.body": "From draft, send-to-review requires more than one course attendee (memberCount > 1) and moves to review queue 215115.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.course-review-actions.title": "Review decisions",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.course-review-actions.body": "In status 215115: mark-as-ok → 215116 approved; send-to-draft returns to 215114; send-to-marfoozeh → 215117 rejected. Un-reject from 215117 back to 215115.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.course-workflow-notes.title": "Required notes",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.course-workflow-notes.body": "Returning to draft or rejecting (marfoozeh) requires an operator note (UI + workflow parity).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.activity-status-register.title": "Registration queue",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.activity-status-register.body": "Activities in status 211311 (register) appear in the registration admin queue excluding central type 213915 when filtered.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.activity-image-limits.title": "Image count",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.activity-image-limits.body": "send-to-waited-1 requires at least one activity file and at most four images; otherwise the action is hidden or rejected server-side.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.activity-workflow-chain.title": "Status chain",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.activity-workflow-chain.body": "211311 register → 211312 initial documentation → 211313 final documentation → 211314 completed. Return to register from 211312/211313 with note. Reject from final doc to 211315 marfoozeh.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.activity-marfoozeh.title": "Un-reject activity",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.activity-marfoozeh.body": "send-to-un-marfoozeh from 211315 restores final documentation queue 211313.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.self-announce-window.title": "Time window",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.self-announce-window.body": "Self-announcement must be enabled, activity not completed, and current time within nbWindowStartAt / nbWindowEndAt when those are set.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.self-announce-metadata.title": "Required submission",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.self-announce-metadata.body": "Member must supply GPS lat/lon and selfie; device OS/id/datetime recorded or required per policy.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.self-announce-central-device.title": "Central activities",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.self-announce-central-device.body": "Central activity type 213915 (or explicit requireSubmissionDeviceMetadata) mandates device fields, not optional record-only.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.targhin-queues.title": "Admin queues",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.targhin-queues.body": "Primary path: create request (hwy_targhin_create_request) + admin decide (hwy_targhin_decide_request). Direct apply/remove is documented under targhin-direct-sp — not a second TS mutation path.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.targhin-reason-vocab.title": "Decision reasons",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.targhin-reason-vocab.body": "Approve reasons from Base Info parent 212130; reject reasons from parent 212170 — both required on final decision.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.targhin-nego-notes.title": "Negotiation notes",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.targhin-nego-notes.body": "Adding a targhin note in dossier requires at least 20 characters; nego thread uses legacy actor username resolution.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.org-transfer-institutes.title": "Institute allow-list",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.org-transfer-institutes.body": "Only configured institutes (hemam, mehani, ashaaer, mithaaq, nokhab, alforat) expose org transfer request actions.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.org-transfer-roles.title": "Request roles",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.org-transfer-roles.body": "Each institute maps to a legacy request role (e.g. HWY_R_1000079 for hemam); ADMIN bypasses and can act for all. Member search results for transfer use the same identity masks as the directory (see identity-masks).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-defs-institute.title": "Institute lists",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-defs-institute.body": "listLogicCode institute binds a nav list to hwy_institutes.id and member_institutes membership rules.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-defs-predicate.title": "Predicate lists",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-defs-predicate.body": "Predicate lists reference predicateRef (legacy SQL/view name) for conditional member sets such as waited queues or targhin status. Waited_1 / Waited_2 map to membership_status_code filters — actions are documented under membership-approval-pipeline.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-sp-decisions.title": "Stored procedures only",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-sp-decisions.body": "Call center and local decisions mutate membership_status_code only through hwy_membership_apply_call_center_decision and hwy_membership_apply_local_decision (/api/hwy/membership/*). No multi-step membership SQL in Node services.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-status-transitions.title": "Status transitions",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-status-transitions.body": "Call center: approve pending_call_center → pending_local; reject → rejected_call_center; unreject → pending_call_center. Local: approve pending_local → active (sets membership_on and, when user_id is null, allocates username + base_users in the same transaction); reject_final → rejected_local_verification; reject_returnable → rejected_local; unreject from rejected_* → pending_local. Status codes are Base Info short names (Membership Status).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-local-activation-account.title": "Platform account on local approve",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-local-activation-account.body": "When activation runs, Node generates a random five-digit password, hashes it with bcrypt, and passes password_hash to dbo.hwy_membership_apply_local_decision. The procedure inserts base_users (username from repo, placeholder email member-{id}@member.hawiety.local, mobile from phone1). Plain password is not returned on the decision API — legacy activation SMS with @UserName/@Password is not wired yet; assign member platform roles separately if required.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-change-log-not-port.title": "No Members_LogChanges port",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-change-log-not-port.body": "Field history uses platform record events + hwy_member_directory_patch / dossier change log — legacy Members_LogChanges is not duplicated.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-decision-reasons.title": "Reason combo + note",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-decision-reasons.body": "Reject requires a Base Info reason (Membership Call Center / Local Approve or Reject Reason categories) plus a mandatory explanation. The note is stored on hwy_member_notes with subject call_center or local_verification; membership status changes emit platform record events (not Members_LogChanges).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-after-create-hook.title": "After create (self-registration)",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-after-create-hook.body": "After self-registration files are saved, dbo.hwy_member_after_create mirrors applicant note into hwy_member_notes (membership subject), assigns channel institute auto-join when configured, sets tosigh_confirm_code, builds legacy template 111255 SMS with tracking token = member id, and the server sends via platform sendSms (subject 111225). Resend uses hwy_member_after_create_resend + POST /api/hwy/membership/:id/resend-registration-sms. This hook does not allocate التياري or create base_users.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-dossier-ui.title": "Studio UI surface",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-dossier-ui.body": "Waited_1 / Waited_2 designer lists filter by membership_status_code; approve/reject also appear as a Review column on waited list grids. Full actions (unreject, nakhebin family/eghtera/roghe/addr, kasb, institute invite) run from the member dossier (decision dialog: reason combo + required note on reject).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-ops-deferred.title": "Deferred / ops-only",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.membership-ops-deferred.body": "B11 approval-flow dashboard stats: not shipped (read proc optional later). B10 legacy member id link: dbo.hwy_member_legacy_identity_link — cutover/ETL only, no day-to-day Studio UI.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.nakhebin-sp-family.title": "Nakhebin SP family",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.nakhebin-sp-family.body": "Link, family, eghtera, clear, change roghe (nakhebin_link_region_id), and set_addr_eghtera are dbo.hwy_member_nakhebin_* / hwy_member_set_addr_eghtera — invoked from /api/hwy/member-nakhebin/*.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.nakhebin-link-type-vocab.title": "Link type vocabulary",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.nakhebin-link-type-vocab.body": "nakhebin_link_type_code references Base Info Nakhebin Link Type (ballot, family, electoral_center, …). Default ballot on simple link; family link sets family_code; eghtera link sets electoral_center type.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.nakhebin-dossier-ui.title": "Dossier nakhebin section",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.nakhebin-dossier-ui.body": "Read-only nakhebin panels on dossier view; nakhebin section exposes ballot/family/eghtera link, clear, change roghe, and set electoral address via /api/hwy/member-nakhebin/* (no inline TS field patch).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.nakhebin-no-logchanges-port.title": "Nakhebin audit",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.nakhebin-no-logchanges-port.body": "Nakhebin mutations emit the same member field history as dossier patch (nakhebin_id, link type, region, family_code).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.targhin-direct-sp.title": "Direct targhin (legacy MakeTarghin)",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.targhin-direct-sp.body": "Targhin without a request (legacy MakeTarghinById) is not offered. Admin remove-from-dossier uses hwy_targhin_remove_direct; apply uses the request + decide_request path only.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.org-transfer-rollback.title": "Transfer rollback",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.org-transfer-rollback.body": "Org membership invite rollback uses dbo.hwy_org_membership_transfer_rollback (DELETE hwy_member_institutes row) via /api/hwy/org-membership-transfer/.../rollback — same MERGE contract as request.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.org-institute-invite-respond.title": "Invite accept / reject",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.org-institute-invite-respond.body": "Legacy SuggestForOrg / MakeMemberOfOrg: pending row from hwy_org_membership_transfer_request; member accept/reject via hwy_member_institute_respond_invite (member_accepted, institute status active/removed).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.org-employment-clear.title": "Clear org employment",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.org-employment-clear.body": "RemoveEmployeement maps to hwy_member_institute_clear_employment on hwy_member_institutes.current_org_employment_* (General Assembly row).",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.member-kasb-link.title": "Kasb (referrer) link",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.member-kasb-link.body": "AddKasb maps to hwy_member_kasb_link — stores kasb member username on second_referrer_username with optional referrer_relation_id.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.role-electoral-multiple-roles.title": "Multiple roles per person",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.role-electoral-multiple-roles.body": "One member MAY hold several operational roles at once (different role_name / official slots / access bundles). Role count is not limited by this contract.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.role-electoral-single-anchor.title": "Single level and single node (shared)",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.role-electoral-single-anchor.body": "All electoral-tree-scoped roles for that member MUST share exactly one geo_level (province, ghavateh, circle, maktab, region) and exactly one node (legacy_geo_id + geo_base_info_id). A member MUST NOT hold two approved anchors on different levels or nodes at the same time — even with multiple roles. Extra roles attach to the same anchor; moves use nomination / removal workflows — not a second branch on the tree.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.role-electoral-out-of-scope.title": "What this does not cover",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.role-electoral-out-of-scope.body": "Plain membership without an electoral-tree role; nakhebin electoral join on the dossier (membership geography, not official anchoring); institute org membership unless product explicitly binds that role to a geo node.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.role-electoral-enforcement-gap.title": "Enforcement today",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.role-electoral-enforcement-gap.body": "Target writes: hwy_geo_responsibility_* and hwy_member_area_limits must enforce single-anchor when extended. Install script hwy_geo_responsibility_member_area_limits MERGE-syncs area-limit rows from Studio nomination requests (one row per member_id + legacy_geo_id) but does not yet collapse multiple nodes to one anchor. ETL/legacy can still leave several approved nodes per member. Treat multi-anchor as drift — new geo/role work should block or replace a second anchor and update this rule when runtime matches.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-legacy-filter-scope.title": "When mode 2 applies",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-legacy-filter-scope.body": "Every Hawiety member-directory people list whose legacy scope starts with HWY_Members_List_ uses HwyMemberDirectoryLegacyFieldByFieldPanel when the legacy field toggle is on — except quick-search picker AlMontadhemin_SingleView. Wizard pickers (similar-members bar, etc.) keep their own compact filters.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-legacy-filter-panel-rows.title": "Locked row order",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-legacy-filter-panel-rows.body": "Row 1 = page logic (All People: membership status checkboxes; Montadhemin: institute multi-filter; image-fix: queue filters). Row 2 = identity (gender → membership id → phone → four name fields). Row 3 = personal details (join-tasjil state → national id → birth year). Row 4 = education/work selects. Row 5 = electoral center cascade (memberRashh parity). Optional extraRows below for list-specific dates/flags.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-legacy-filter-membership-id.title": "Membership id search mode",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-legacy-filter-membership-id.body": "Per list, membershipIdentifierSearchMode is username, trackingCode, or usernameOrTrackingCode (All People default). usernameOrTrackingCode writes the same value to gridToolbar.legacy.username and trackingCode; list API ORs when both match. Server: buildHwyMemberDirectoryListLegacyFilterWhere.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-legacy-filter-join-tasjil.title": "Registration status (join tasjil)",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-legacy-filter-join-tasjil.body": "Row 3 select hwy.members.legacyFilter.joinTasjilState maps registered_biometric / unregistered to Base Info ids on nakhebin_join_tasjil_state_code. Store gridToolbar.filters.nakhebinJoinTasjilStateCode; API filter[nakhebinJoinTasjilStateCode][eq]; fast path hwyMemberDirectoryListFastPath when only this filter is active.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-legacy-filter-server-where.title": "Server filter compilation",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.list-legacy-filter-server-where.body": "Legacy toolbar keys and gridToolbar.filters.* compile to SQL via hwyMemberDirectoryListLegacyFilterWhere.service and list scope rules in hwyMemberDirectoryListScope.service. Identity masks still run after enrichment (applyHwyMemberIdentityFieldMasksToRows) — filters do not bypass HashPhones.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.employees-list-access.title": "Portal access",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.employees-list-access.body": "pageKey hwy-employees-list. Route middleware resolves allow roles from legacy HWY_Members.Read_Employees via fetchLegacyPlatformRolesByAction; ADMIN always allowed. Fallback to ADMIN when legacy role DB is unreachable.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.employees-list-read-path.title": "Read path",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.employees-list-read-path.body": "SQL Server: dbo.hwy_employees_list_read and hwy_employees_list_count with params from buildHwyEmployeesListProcParams (legacy filter mapping). When legacy import parity is not ready, falls back to queryLegacyEmployeesList* against the legacy DB. List scope legacy hint HWY_Members_List_AlMontadhemin for enrichment.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.employees-list-masks.title": "Identity masks on rows",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.employees-list-masks.body": "Rows pass through enrichHwyMemberDirectoryListRows then the same viewer gender / institute masks as member directory lists. Limit columns (rolesLimits, areasLimits, genderLimits, orgLimits, …) are display-only legacy parity fields on the grid.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.geo-resp-studio-path.title": "Geo responsibility Studio",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.geo-resp-studio-path.body": "Nomination, approval, removal, and official access use hwy_geo_responsibility_* procedures and hwy_geo_responsibility_requests — not legacy per-level H_* SP writes.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.geo-legacy-sp-retired.title": "Legacy geo SPs",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.geo-legacy-sp-retired.body": "H_Circle_*, H_Tamvin_*, H_Eghtera_*, H_Mohafezat_*, H_Mahatteh_*, H_Ghavateh_* suggest/approve/remove SPs and ChangeMasooliatPlace / UpdateFlags are retired at cutover — Studio geo responsibility is the only write path.",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.geo-officials-reports-deferred.title": "Officials reports (deferred)",
  "hwy.businessRules.rule.geo-officials-reports-deferred.body": "Legacy Masoolin_TopOfficials / BelowOfficials read/report SPs are not ported in Phase 1; optional read procs or reports may follow later.",
